# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Ali Rajabpour et al. (2025). Accurate estimation of interfacial thermal conductance between silicon and diamond enabled by a machine learning interatomic potential.
#   International Journal of Thermal Sciences. doi:10.1016/j.ijthermalsci.2025.109876  arXiv:2407.15404v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2407.15404v1 (sha256 deae1719299b3dc4...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 394 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/rajabpour2025.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the PBEsol AIMD data (Si/diamond heterostructure,
# pure diamond and pure silicon, heated from 1 to 2000 K; 9,000
# configurations), the two-step passive MTP fit (first MTP on 800
# configurations; final MTP after adding high-extrapolation-grade
# configurations; 409 parameters, 4 A cutoff), and the NEMD use. No
# training or test errors are stated in the main text; interfacial
# conductances and spectral analyses are properties.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
